{
  "project_id": 22,
  "project_label": "gemma",
  "task_id": 10053,
  "title": "The hidden power of smiling",
  "author": "Ron Gutman",
  "url": "https://www.ted.com/talks/ron_gutman_the_hidden_power_of_smiling",
  "annotation_id": null,
  "completed_by": 7,
  "created_at": "2026-05-07T05:07:06.715714Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-05-07T05:07:06.715714Z",
  "lead_time": 49.118,
  "result": [
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "0",
        "end": "0",
        "startOffset": 44,
        "endOffset": 53,
        "text": "superhero",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "FIG"
        ]
      },
      "id": "C75E62E17A",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "0",
        "end": "0",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 54,
        "text": "When I was a child, I always wanted to be a superhero.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "D71E68167A",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "1",
        "end": "1",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 51,
        "text": "I wanted to save the world and make everyone happy.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "A4918A70B2",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "2",
        "end": "2",
        "startOffset": 40,
        "endOffset": 64,
        "text": "make my dreams come true",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "FIG"
        ]
      },
      "id": "D7545D219B",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "2",
        "end": "2",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 65,
        "text": "But I knew that I'd need superpowers to make my dreams come true.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "20481F5D9E",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "3",
        "end": "3",
        "startOffset": 29,
        "endOffset": 47,
        "text": "imaginary journeys",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "FIG"
        ]
      },
      "id": "39FBE566A4",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "3",
        "end": "3",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 152,
        "text": "So I used to embark on these imaginary journeys to find intergalactic objects from planet Krypton, which was a lot of fun, but didn't yield much result.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "7A7C4C4313",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "4",
        "end": "4",
        "startOffset": 121,
        "endOffset": 144,
        "text": "journey of real science",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "FIG"
        ]
      },
      "id": "C430D52E25",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "4",
        "end": "4",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 174,
        "text": "When I grew up and realized that science fiction was not a good source for superpowers, I decided instead to embark on a journey of real science, to find a more useful truth.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "D2378F91F9",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "5",
        "end": "5",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 211,
        "text": "I started my journey in California, with a UC Berkeley 30-year longitudinal study that examined the photos of students in an old yearbook, and tried to measure their success and well-being throughout their life.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "7C3F12FCD1",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "6",
        "end": "6",
        "startOffset": 60,
        "endOffset": 129,
        "text": "predict how fulfilling and long-lasting a subject's marriage would be",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "FIG"
        ]
      },
      "id": "3FB4674D23",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "6",
        "end": "6",
        "startOffset": 212,
        "endOffset": 244,
        "text": "inspiring she would be to others",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "FIG"
        ]
      },
      "id": "1518060FA0",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "6",
        "end": "6",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 245,
        "text": "By measuring the students' smiles, researchers were able to predict how fulfilling and long-lasting a subject's marriage would be, (Laughter) how well she would score on standardized tests of well-being, and how inspiring she would be to others.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "771684590B",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "7",
        "end": "7",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 59,
        "text": "In another yearbook, I stumbled upon Barry Obama's picture.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "906061F402",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "8",
        "end": "8",
        "startOffset": 49,
        "endOffset": 87,
        "text": "superpowers came from his super collar",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "FIG"
        ]
      },
      "id": "A89FC61918",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "8",
        "end": "8",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 88,
        "text": "When I first saw his picture, I thought that his superpowers came from his super collar.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "CEDB57EB67",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "9",
        "end": "9",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 50,
        "text": "(Laughter) But now I know it was all in his smile.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "D03BE0F00B",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "10",
        "end": "10",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 143,
        "text": "Another aha! moment came from a 2010 Wayne State University research project that looked into pre-1950s baseball cards of Major League players.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "6AA032699A",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "11",
        "end": "11",
        "startOffset": 31,
        "endOffset": 99,
        "text": "span of a player's smile could actually predict the span of his life",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "FIG"
        ]
      },
      "id": "396921DEF6",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "11",
        "end": "11",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 100,
        "text": "The researchers found that the span of a player's smile could actually predict the span of his life.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "982810D057",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "12",
        "end": "12",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 150,
        "text": "Players who didn't smile in their pictures lived an average of only 72.9 years, where players with beaming smiles lived an average of almost 80 years.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "C8FA89D579",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "13",
        "end": "13",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 61,
        "text": "(Laughter) The good news is that we're actually born smiling.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "30A72B14DC",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "14",
        "end": "14",
        "startOffset": 52,
        "endOffset": 85,
        "text": "developing babies appear to smile",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "FIG"
        ]
      },
      "id": "64DF7AFCDE",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "14",
        "end": "14",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 104,
        "text": "Using 3D ultrasound technology, we can now see that developing babies appear to smile, even in the womb.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "E5D1E74969",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "15",
        "end": "15",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 80,
        "text": "When they're born, babies continue to smile -- initially, mostly in their sleep.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "522BC28F62",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "16",
        "end": "16",
        "startOffset": 22,
        "endOffset": 59,
        "text": "smile to the sound of the human voice",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "FIG"
        ]
      },
      "id": "EBE43655E7",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "17",
        "end": "17",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 81,
        "text": "Smiling is one of the most basic, biologically uniform expressions of all humans.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "C150714C1B",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "18",
        "end": "18",
        "startOffset": 338,
        "endOffset": 353,
        "text": "you and I would",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "ENG"
        ]
      },
      "id": "8D0B756653",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "18",
        "end": "18",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 354,
        "text": "In studies conducted in Papua New Guinea, Paul Ekman, the world’s most renowned researcher on facial expressions, found that even members of the Fore tribe, who were completely disconnected from Western culture, and also known for their unusual cannibalism rituals, (Laughter) attributed smiles to descriptions of situations the same way you and I would.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "EA66F78F83",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "19",
        "end": "19",
        "startOffset": 38,
        "endOffset": 49,
        "text": "all the way",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "REP"
        ]
      },
      "id": "E03DA35A1E",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "19",
        "end": "19",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 139,
        "text": "So from Papua New Guinea to Hollywood all the way to modern art in Beijing, we smile often, and use smiles to express joy and satisfaction.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "13233A549C",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "20",
        "end": "20",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 67,
        "text": "How many people here in this room smile more than 20 times per day?",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "ENG"
        ]
      },
      "id": "66E2465FE3",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "21",
        "end": "21",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 26,
        "text": "Raise your hand if you do.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "ENG"
        ]
      },
      "id": "44418366EA",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "22",
        "end": "22",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 8,
        "text": "Oh, wow.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "3F26A25233",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "23",
        "end": "23",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 136,
        "text": "Outside of this room, more than a third of us smile more than 20 times per day, whereas less than 14 percent of us smile less than five.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "B1AAE2AE09",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "24",
        "end": "24",
        "startOffset": 24,
        "endOffset": 48,
        "text": "most amazing superpowers",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "HUMOR"
        ]
      },
      "id": "1B4973760E",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "24",
        "end": "24",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 111,
        "text": "In fact, those with the most amazing superpowers are actually children, who smile as many as 400 times per day.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "D27397075E",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "25",
        "end": "25",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 22,
        "text": "Have you ever wondered",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "ENG"
        ]
      },
      "id": "6095DFF345",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "25",
        "end": "25",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 102,
        "text": "Have you ever wondered why being around children, who smile so frequently, makes you smile very often?",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "A6A048F94C",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "26",
        "end": "26",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 122,
        "text": "A recent study at Uppsala University in Sweden found that it's very difficult to frown when looking at someone who smiles.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "25AD21DCED",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "27",
        "end": "27",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 12,
        "text": "You ask why?",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "ENG"
        ]
      },
      "id": "E92611E5C2",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "28",
        "end": "28",
        "startOffset": 19,
        "endOffset": 44,
        "text": "evolutionarily contagious",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "FIG"
        ]
      },
      "id": "D398EE802A",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "28",
        "end": "28",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 114,
        "text": "Because smiling is evolutionarily contagious, and it suppresses the control we usually have on our facial muscles.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "BE95351895",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "29",
        "end": "29",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 159,
        "text": "Mimicking a smile and experiencing it physically helps us understand whether our smile is fake or real, so we can understand the emotional state of the smiler,",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "A30A171F6D",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "30",
        "end": "30",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 208,
        "text": "In a recent mimicking study at the University of Clermont-Ferrand in France, subjects were asked to determine whether a smile was real or fake while holding a pencil in their mouth to repress smiling muscles.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "17ADAF39B2",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "31",
        "end": "31",
        "startOffset": 52,
        "endOffset": 166,
        "text": "but with the pencil in their mouth -- when they could not mimic the smile they saw -- their judgment was impaired.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "REP"
        ]
      },
      "id": "EAC30F2FCE",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "32",
        "end": "32",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 140,
        "text": "(Laughter) In addition to theorizing on evolution in \"The Origin of Species,\" Charles Darwin also wrote the facial feedback response theory.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "1516652B71",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "33",
        "end": "33",
        "startOffset": 23,
        "endOffset": 78,
        "text": "the act of smiling itself actually makes us feel better",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "FIG"
        ]
      },
      "id": "A13D6DB6E4",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "33",
        "end": "33",
        "startOffset": 92,
        "endOffset": 137,
        "text": "smiling being merely a result of feeling good",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "REP"
        ]
      },
      "id": "C6117A8160",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "34",
        "end": "34",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 151,
        "text": "In his study, Darwin actually cited a French neurologist, Guillaume Duchenne, who sent electric jolts to facial muscles to induce and stimulate smiles.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "F407DFDED9",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "35",
        "end": "35",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 31,
        "text": "Please, don't try this at home.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "HUMOR"
        ]
      },
      "id": "5F31B307A0",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "36",
        "end": "36",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 155,
        "text": "(Laughter) In a related German study, researchers used fMRI imaging to measure brain activity before and after injecting Botox to suppress smiling muscles.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "3FCC615BB5",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "37",
        "end": "37",
        "startOffset": 55,
        "endOffset": 186,
        "text": "facial feedback modifies the neural processing of emotional content in the brain, in a way that helps us feel better when we smile.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "FIG"
        ]
      },
      "id": "D00ACF375B",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "38",
        "end": "38",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 127,
        "text": "Smiling stimulates our brain reward mechanism in a way that even chocolate -- a well-regarded pleasure inducer -- cannot match.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "FIG"
        ]
      },
      "id": "26EBABE159",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "39",
        "end": "39",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 123,
        "text": "British researchers found that one smile can generate the same level of brain stimulation as up to 2,000 bars of chocolate.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "3AACB604D6",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "40",
        "end": "40",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 121,
        "text": "(Laughter) Wait -- The same study found that smiling is as stimulating as receiving up to 16,000 pounds sterling in cash.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "E60542D7DC",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "41",
        "end": "41",
        "startOffset": 11,
        "endOffset": 40,
        "text": "That's like 25 grand a smile.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "HUMOR"
        ]
      },
      "id": "2885ED2A40",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "42",
        "end": "42",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 13,
        "text": "It's not bad.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "C64E95C1F9",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "43",
        "end": "43",
        "startOffset": 29,
        "endOffset": 112,
        "text": "25,000 times 400 -- quite a few kids out there feel like Mark Zuckerberg every day.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "FIG"
        ]
      },
      "id": "7DABA5414D",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "44",
        "end": "44",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 89,
        "text": "(Laughter) And unlike lots of chocolate, lots of smiling can actually make you healthier.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "E2FC55B37E",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "45",
        "end": "45",
        "startOffset": 37,
        "endOffset": 62,
        "text": "stress-enhancing hormones",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "FIG"
        ]
      },
      "id": "BB0A70E2F9",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "45",
        "end": "45",
        "startOffset": 125,
        "endOffset": 148,
        "text": "mood-enhancing hormones",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "FIG"
        ]
      },
      "id": "EC08B5BD1D",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "45",
        "end": "45",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 200,
        "text": "Smiling can help reduce the level of stress-enhancing hormones like cortisol, adrenaline and dopamine, increase the level of mood-enhancing hormones like endorphins, and reduce overall blood pressure.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "A653CF5449",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "46",
        "end": "46",
        "startOffset": 7,
        "endOffset": 24,
        "text": "that's not enough",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "ENG"
        ]
      },
      "id": "5ACEB117C8",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "46",
        "end": "46",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 88,
        "text": "And if that's not enough, smiling can actually make you look good in the eyes of others.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "2DC3AB63FA",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "47",
        "end": "47",
        "startOffset": 56,
        "endOffset": 65,
        "text": "you smile",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "ENG"
        ]
      },
      "id": "410FE61814",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "47",
        "end": "47",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 168,
        "text": "A recent study at Penn State University found that when you smile, you don't only appear to be more likable and courteous, but you actually appear to be more competent.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "F0EC20DA17",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "48",
        "end": "48",
        "startOffset": 69,
        "endOffset": 71,
        "text": "or",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "REP"
        ]
      },
      "id": "5BBF52000C",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "48",
        "end": "48",
        "startOffset": 69,
        "endOffset": 71,
        "text": "or",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "REP"
        ]
      },
      "id": "4F04A409E3",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "48",
        "end": "48",
        "startOffset": 69,
        "endOffset": 71,
        "text": "or",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "REP"
        ]
      },
      "id": "77BE57EF5C",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "48",
        "end": "48",
        "startOffset": 98,
        "endOffset": 196,
        "text": "feel as if you just had a whole stack of high-quality chocolate without incurring the caloric cost",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "HUMOR"
        ]
      },
      "id": "94309EC094",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "48",
        "end": "48",
        "startOffset": 201,
        "endOffset": 279,
        "text": "as if you found 25 grand in a pocket of an old jacket you hadn't worn for ages",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "HUMOR"
        ]
      },
      "id": "81F55B147E",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "48",
        "end": "48",
        "startOffset": 305,
        "endOffset": 326,
        "text": "tap into a superpower",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "FIG"
        ]
      },
      "id": "8CD24C6484",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "48",
        "end": "48",
        "startOffset": 0,
        "endOffset": 416,
        "text": "So whenever you want to look great and competent, reduce your stress or improve your marriage, or feel as if you just had a whole stack of high-quality chocolate without incurring the caloric cost, or as if you found 25 grand in a pocket of an old jacket you hadn't worn for ages, or whenever you want to tap into a superpower that will help you and everyone around you live a longer, healthier, happier life, smile.",
        "paragraphlabels": [
          "NONE"
        ]
      },
      "id": "EF9FCBC312",
      "from_name": "label",
      "to_name": "text",
      "type": "paragraphlabels",
      "origin": "manual"
    },
    {
      "value": {
        "start": "49",
